          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: lo sciopero",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "lo sciopero — \"the strike\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Domani c'è lo sciopero dei treni. Tomorrow there is a train strike."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Essere in sciopero — to be on strike. Strikes are announced in advance, so check before you travel."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "sciopero is built on scioperare, usually traced to a Vulgar Latin exoperāre \"to be out of work\", from ex- \"out of\" and operāre \"to work\", built on opus, operis \"work\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
