          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "turno came into Italian from French, from the family of tourner \"to turn\" (EtymDB), which goes back to Latin tornāre \"to turn on a lathe\" (Lewis & Short), from tornus \"a lathe\", a Greek word: work goes round in turns."
            }
          ]
        },
